es/sase-zn/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reclaim athena now and move SASE_TMPDIR off tmpfs and out of [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]Syncthing[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]host-relief[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]host-relief: reclaim the two 31 GB scratch piles on athena, relocate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SASE_TMPDIR out of the Syncthing-synced tree, and capture a documented [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]before/after responsiveness baseline the later phases measure against.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Replace the artifact-index N+1 reconcile and full [/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]dismissed-table rewrite[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]index-core-sql[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]index-core-sql: in the linked sase-core repo, turn the per-candidate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconcile queries into set-based SQL and make the dismissed-identity [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]projection a diff-based upsert instead of an unconditional 46k-row table[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]replace.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop re-parsing the whole notification store on every refresh [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]tick[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]notif-snapshot[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]notif-snapshot: cache the parsed notification snapshot against a cheap [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]change token and bound the active notifications.jsonl so a 13.6 MB [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-parse stops running on the TUI refresh cadence.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bound retained child-process output in the session proc [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]reporter[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]stream-bound[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]stream-bound: cap the unbounded in-memory output list in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]_stream_subprocess and stop mirroring the whole stream into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]operation-request.json records that reached 40 MB each.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Narrow the artifact-index lock and stop authoritative syncs [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]bypassing the signature check[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]index-tui-cadence[dim] · [dim][/dim]after index-core-sql[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]index-tui-cadence: keep interactive index reads off the long maintenance[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lock and let authoritative dismissed-projection syncs short-circuit on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]an unchanged signature the same way non-authoritative ones already do.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Extend scratch hygiene to agent-created build directories and [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]disk pressure[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]tmp-hygiene[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host-relief[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tmp-hygiene: give agent-created cargo/build scratch a managed home the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reaper can actually see, and add size-aware pressure reaping so a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]multi-gigabyte directory is not held for a purely time-based horizon.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Attribute and fix the residual ACE heap growth[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]heap-attrib[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host-relief, stream-bound[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]heap-attrib: add an opt-in heap sampler for the long-lived TUI, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]attribute whatever remains of the ~12.5 GB anonymous heap after the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bounded-stream fix, and fix the retained-object sites it names.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Re-measure on athena against explicit responsiveness targets[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after index-tui-cadence, notif-snapshot, tmp-hygiene, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]heap-attrib[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify: re-run the documented capture recipe on athena under real agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]load and confirm the keystroke, CPU, and RSS targets hold, recording the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]result in the perf runbook.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-zn","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-zn.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-636ddd1e9ebd88c8ea98b71b00396d5d","started_at":"2026-09-11T19:37:06.685423+00:00","state":"failed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"3032a16baaed9d1afe80f25ab6640c72229d4a3aee13e3ea010acf216ed346c3","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-zn.6/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"8a2bec5a57359705790f28affe35aee4c5b4adb7ed71f924771f2a9804d3d9bc","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-zn.6/meta.json","size_bytes":633},"prompt":{"digest":"c73d35b3b6b50c119720a77383e8ffc561baa16153c76dfbf5c84e51d539113f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-zn.6/prompt.md","size_bytes":141},"state":{"digest":"22d44838c981